    pr_ref:  # 6a63
    description: "Surfaced by the WI-tosul dead-code re-measure (2026-07-07, lab notebook wi_tosul_deadcode_remeasure_07072026.md). Across 4 polyglot repos the ONLY consistent dead-code over-flagger is the '?' (no-language) cohort at ~100% dead: kserve 60, prometheus 180, killbill 49. Concentrated in .go (142/180 on prometheus) + .ts/.tsx (38). Two sub-issues: (1) LANGUAGE-STAMP GAP — the node id encodes the language but Symbol.language is None (an axis/identity inconsistency: the id-slot language and the language field disagree); (2) SPURIOUS EXTRACTION — some are non-functions mis-emitted as kind=function (Go 'case', inline closures with names like 'r'/'ctx', single-line spans). Fix (1): find the producer(s) emitting language=None function/method nodes and stamp the language (derivable from the id-slot / file extension), + a validator that Symbol.language is non-None for any node whose kind is function/method. Fix (2) is a separate go/ts extraction-precision concern. Small volume (~50-180/repo) but systematic. NOT the WI-tosul monoculture (that is discharged) — a distinct data-quality gap."  # 6a63
    fields:  # 6a63
      statement: "Every function/method node whose id encodes a language carries a non-None Symbol.language, so dead-code/reachability can match it to seeds."  # 6a63
      root_cause: "Some function/method nodes are emitted with Symbol.language=None even though their id embeds the language (e.g. id 'go:web/api/v1/api.go:1982:notifications:function' but language field is None). Nodes without a language can't be matched to language-scoped seeds/entrypoints, so dead-code-maybe flags them ~100% dead. Producer(s) unknown — likely a secondary pass / linker / specific construct (inline funcs, closures) that skips the language stamp. A subset are also spurious extractions (Go 'case' keyword, one-line closures named 'r'/'ctx')."  # 6a63
